Body:
> There is a upstream pending PR ([NixOS/nixpkgs#494267](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/494267)) for bun upgrade, here I give a quick workaround for flake project:
> 
> {
>   inputs = {
>     bun-unstable.url = "github:arch-fan/nixpkgs/bun-1.3.10";
>     opencode = {
>       url = "github:anomalyco/opencode/v1.2.15";
>       inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "bun-unstable";
>     };
>   };
> }
> 
> Not sure adding a pinned bun version in the flake project is best practice or not, I think adding it here may make build cache invalidated and will fetch bun binary every time even upstream PR merged into the nixpkgs repository.

You're right, pinning the version wouldn't be great; unless the derivation from that url was cached? I'm not solid enough on the caching mechanics myself to go to bat for that. The second suggested option might be good unless the  project is explicitly leaning on features only available in the lastest version of bun? I think they both would *work*, but I'm not in position to determine if the juice would be worth the squeeze. So I didn't go ahead and make a PR, though I figured I'd report what I saw happening and leave them to be assessed as suggestions.

@LazyYuuki does this change resolve your issue? In order for the effect to work, I believe you will also need to go into you `opencode.json` and expicitly set

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permissions": {
    "edit": "ask"
  },
  ...
}
```
